# The builder stage does `COPY . .`, so without this the whole of `target/` --
# gigabytes of host-platform artifacts that Linux cannot use and would rebuild
# anyway -- is uploaded into the build context on every build.
#
# `mise run docker:ignore-verify` is the gate for this file: it builds an
# ephemeral image, lists the context, and fails if anything below leaks in or if
# a file the build genuinely needs was excluded.

# Build output. The single largest win.
target/
target-linux/

# VCS and CI. Nothing in the image build reads these.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Docs and tooling that never reach a binary.
docs/
scripts/
worktrees/
supply-chain/
.rumdl_cache/
.remember/
.claude/
.act/

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Coverage and profiling artifacts, all regenerated.
cobertura.xml
lcov.info
results.sarif
tarpaulin-report.html
tarpaulin-report.json
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# Repository tooling config. None of it is read during an image build: the
# builder runs `cargo build`, not clippy, rustfmt, hk, comply or mise.
mise.toml
mise.local.toml
hk.pkl
deny.toml
REUSE.toml
rustfmt.toml
.clippy.toml
tomlfmt.toml
taplo.toml
.env

# All markdown. The `readme = "README.md"` KEY is package metadata, read by
# `cargo package`/`publish` and never by `cargo build` -- but that is not the
# only thing that reads the file.
#
# `crates/comply/src/lib.rs` carries `#![doc = include_str!("../README.md")]`,
# and `include_str!` is expanded by rustc during compilation, so a plain
# `cargo build` needs the file on disk. Excluding it failed the builder stage
# with "couldn't read crates/comply/src/../README.md: No such file or
# directory". The dependencies stage was unaffected -- it `touch`es an empty
# placeholder lib.rs -- so the break only surfaced after `COPY . .`.
#
# Negation must FOLLOW the exclusion: last matching rule wins.
**/*.md
DCO.txt
!crates/*/README.md

# The Dockerfiles themselves are read by the builder, not copied into a stage.
Dockerfile
Test.Dockerfile
.dockerignore
